# Frontend / Next.js

## Component Model

- **Server Components by default**: Do not add `"use client"` unless the component uses hooks, browser APIs, or event handlers
- **Feature folders**: Colocate components with their feature; shared UI goes in `components/`
- **Type props**: Define interfaces for component props; avoid `any`

## Styling and Layout

- **Tailwind only**: Use Tailwind classes; avoid inline styles except for dynamic values
- **Responsive**: Mobile-first; use `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` breakpoints so UI adapts to screen size
- **Theme consistency**: Prefer `globals.css` variables or a central `lib/theme.ts` for colors and spacing

## Assets and Data

- **Images**: Use Next.js `Image` for images; set `alt`, `width`, `height` (or fill)
- **API calls**: Use route handlers, server actions, or a dedicated API layer; type responses from backend

## Example

```tsx
// Server Component (default) — no "use client"
export default async function DocList() {
  const docs = await getDocs();
  return <DocGrid items={docs} />;
}

// Client only when needed
"use client";
export function DocGrid({ items }: { items: DocItem[] }) {
  const [selected, setSelected] = useState<string | null>(null);
  return (/* ... */);
}
```
